    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1958-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\[ 4^x-4^{x-1} =\\frac34\\,4^x=24, \\] so \\(4^x=32.\\) Thus \\(2^{2x}=2^5,\\) giving \\(x=\\frac{5}{2}.\\) Therefore \\[ (2x)^x=5^{\\frac{5}{2}}=25\\sqrt5. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(4^{x-1}\\) from the left side",
        "Once \\(4^x=32,\\) rewrite both sides as powers of \\(2\\)"
      ],
